'''Killer Cats''' are seasonal [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cats]] based on some of the [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]]. They can be obtained from [[Horde of Cats]], which occurs every Cat Day (February 22nd for [[BCJP]], August 8th for other versions).

The Killer Cats' Normal and Evolved Forms are joke characters. Although they recharge very quickly, they cost 7,500¢ and have few or no advantages over their Normal counterparts, making them utterly inefficient. Only the Basic [[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Cat]] has a [[True Form]], which makes him a viable unit by greatly decreasing his cost along with gaining several other improvements.

[[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cat]]'s Killer variant only appears on the [[Killer Axe Cat Base (Enemy Base)|Killer Axe Cat Base]], not as an obtainable unit.

The list of Killer Cats includes:
*[[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Cat]] → True Killer Cat → Radical Cat
**True Form is an [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] tanker with Strong Against, Behemoth Slayer and Immune to [[Surge Attack|Surge]].
*[[Killer Tank Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Tank Cat]] → True Killer Tank Cat
**A carbon copy of [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]].
*[[Killer Gross Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Gross Cat]] → True Killer Gross Cat
**Has double the range of [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]].
*[[Killer Cowbird Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Cowbird Cat]] → True Killer Cowbird Cat
**A fusion of [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]] and [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]] with Long Distance (170~470) and longer standing range than either (270).

==Trivia== 
*Killer Cat and Killer Gross Cat (with shorter legs) appeared in [[Metal Slug Collaboration Event|Metal Slug Defense]] before being added to [[The Battle Cats]], along with a Killer Wall Cat and Killer Titan Cat.

